{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1480589-first-time-homecrafting-an-adversary-and-would-like-help","id":1480589,"title":"First time homecrafting an adversary and would like help.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-05-09T15:58:43-07:00","id":1480589,"title":"First time homecrafting an adversary and would like help.","content":"Hello! For the campaign I am running, I wanted to make an adversary who could be sort of a spylike reoccuring mysterious figure through the campaign at least at origin level. Nobody is quite sure what her motivations are, and they do not seem consistent so one adventure she could be ambushing the party, the next she's seducing one of them to steal a mcguffin, the next she is fighting alongside them. I wanted her to have a sort of spyish edge so I figured I would flavor her as an Heir, since the dragon book outright mentions spy stuff as how a typical campaign would run. As such I figured I would make her a Draq heir of Leviathan. I just finished the stats and want to know if she seems too weak or too powerful. In addition I would like suggestions thinking of a backstory and motivations, so far I just know she is the daughter of an Apache woman and an Arab man (Which is where her Draq blood comes from). I apologize if I have unintentionally done anything offensive, here is the link: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bJgCoOhvC9TzKuCafnpLrbROfmHaXZ4n4pZ497DffuU/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12517-storyteller323","name":"Storyteller323","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-09T16:16:08-07:00","id":1480592,"title":"","content":"Oh, commenting is allowed with the link if you would rather do that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12517-storyteller323","name":"Storyteller323","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-11T14:37:44-07:00","id":1480764,"title":"","content":"I gave you the benefit of the doubt, scrolling through some really... exaggerated and unnecessary images (After page 2 I thought you were just trying a really weird troll to make people look at the art) to find the statblock. So:<br /> <br /> The Dragon Kickstarter preview offers &quot;Rogue Agent&quot; as a Dragon Archetype, matching Villain. It also offers a few Qualities that work for that tier:<br /> <b>One Step Ahead: </b>+2 Speed Scale when escaping/being chased (That means +4 enhancements on the roll)<br /> <b>Shattering Transformation: </b>Spend 1 tension to gain +2e to the Primary pool, +1 Size and Force Scale, Hard Armor 3<br /> Flair:<br /> <b>Step Sideways: </b>Spend 1 tension after the Antagonist suffers damage. The Antagonist disappears from the scene. Tracking requires a Clash of Wills. The Antagonist may return later in the same scene.<br /> <br /> But if you stick with Origin stuff, here's what I see:<br /> 1. The character isn't described as a combat wombat, but everything you've chosen is combat related. Look through the Social Flairs and decide if any of those work for the character, or at least keep them in mind.<br /> 2. At very least, you should add Red Herring as a Flair, in case the players come looking.<br /> 3. The primary/secondary pools are defined with Skills, in a way that limits her. Instead of Skills specifically, stat her out with &quot;Attack from the Shadows&quot; and &quot;Clashes of Will&quot; Primary and &quot;Mysterious Ally&quot; Secondary, or something like that.<br /> 4. The Drive is really specific to the Band. Maybe instead, she is working on her own agenda each time. Think of her Drive as her current Draconic Deed. Maybe the Drive the first time is &quot;delay the Band so they miss their meeting with the Scion of Apollo&quot;. Next time it's &quot;Take the idol before the band does&quot; and the time after that it's &quot;Give the counterfeit statue to the band.&quot;<br /> <br /> Remember that Dragon Heirs are often given tasks that they don't understand, because their Handler's agenda is hidden. Changing the Drive each time they meet illustrates that, and gives you a specific thing for her to do.<br /> <br /> Don't plan to move her from Mysterious Ally to Adversary quickly. Let them get used to seeing her (or evidence of her) around, like she's Moriarty or Lupin. Give her Thousand Faces so they never know who she is, but they keep seeing evidence of her passing (I'm picturing something like wingprints in dust, or talonmarks in a doorway). As long as she stays on the same Tier as the players, she has a good chance of defending against tracking Knacks and other magics, until her Handler's plans come to a peak, and they find themselves in direct opposition to her. But she's also the one who rescued the daughter of Obatala in Tartarus. She was the Canary who died to help us take down the Troll and moved the Scion of Freyr closer to his Wyrd.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23791-ashnak","name":"Ashnak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-11T15:35:44-07:00","id":1480767,"title":"","content":"Could this adversary be a Scion of Nemesis? I realize you were thinking dragon, but that could be a miss direction. Where Nemesis is about justice for those who have avoided earthly justice, this Scion of Nemesis could be about testing those seeking power. Nemesis brought punishment, her sister gave rewards for no reason. This Scion could be about heading off trouble by getting rid of the unworthy before they can create destruction and misery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-11T16:02:28-07:00","id":1480770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashnak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1480589-first-time-homecrafting-an-adversary-and-would-like-help?p=1480764#post1480764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I gave you the benefit of the doubt, scrolling through some really... exaggerated and unnecessary images (After page 2 I thought you were just trying a really weird troll to make people look at the art) to find the statblock. So:<br /> <br /> The Dragon Kickstarter preview offers &quot;Rogue Agent&quot; as a Dragon Archetype, matching Villain. It also offers a few Qualities that work for that tier:<br /> <b>One Step Ahead: </b>+2 Speed Scale when escaping/being chased (That means +4 enhancements on the roll)<br /> <b>Shattering Transformation: </b>Spend 1 tension to gain +2e to the Primary pool, +1 Size and Force Scale, Hard Armor 3<br /> Flair:<br /> <b>Step Sideways: </b>Spend 1 tension after the Antagonist suffers damage. The Antagonist disappears from the scene. Tracking requires a Clash of Wills. The Antagonist may return later in the same scene.<br /> <br /> But if you stick with Origin stuff, here's what I see:<br /> 1. The character isn't described as a combat wombat, but everything you've chosen is combat related. Look through the Social Flairs and decide if any of those work for the character, or at least keep them in mind.<br /> 2. At very least, you should add Red Herring as a Flair, in case the players come looking.<br /> 3. The primary/secondary pools are defined with Skills, in a way that limits her. Instead of Skills specifically, stat her out with &quot;Attack from the Shadows&quot; and &quot;Clashes of Will&quot; Primary and &quot;Mysterious Ally&quot; Secondary, or something like that.<br /> 4. The Drive is really specific to the Band. Maybe instead, she is working on her own agenda each time. Think of her Drive as her current Draconic Deed. Maybe the Drive the first time is &quot;delay the Band so they miss their meeting with the Scion of Apollo&quot;. Next time it's &quot;Take the idol before the band does&quot; and the time after that it's &quot;Give the counterfeit statue to the band.&quot;<br /> <br /> Remember that Dragon Heirs are often given tasks that they don't understand, because their Handler's agenda is hidden. Changing the Drive each time they meet illustrates that, and gives you a specific thing for her to do.<br /> <br /> Don't plan to move her from Mysterious Ally to Adversary quickly. Let them get used to seeing her (or evidence of her) around, like she's Moriarty or Lupin. Give her Thousand Faces so they never know who she is, but they keep seeing evidence of her passing (I'm picturing something like wingprints in dust, or talonmarks in a doorway). As long as she stays on the same Tier as the players, she has a good chance of defending against tracking Knacks and other magics, until her Handler's plans come to a peak, and they find themselves in direct opposition to her. But she's also the one who rescued the daughter of Obatala in Tartarus. She was the Canary who died to help us take down the Troll and moved the Scion of Freyr closer to his Wyrd.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I admit the art is a bit gretuitous, but it's a bit hard to find art of the character (A rule63 version of Geronimo from Fate Grand Order) that looks modest, I was at least trying to find art that made her look badass with the first two, and something at least <i>marginally</i> less fanservice-ey with the third. The gimmick with this campaign is that their pantheons are randomly selected and among the options was titanspawn, which nobody rolled, and dragon, which one of the players DID roll, getting Tiamat as their specific ancestor, hence the character being focused on her.<br /> <br /> 1. Was more trying to go for stealth and combat with the skills, since she's a bit assassin-esque in how she operates: Focusing on stealth, ambushes, manipulation, etc.<br /> 2. That is a good point, one of the players <i>does</i> have worrying hound.<br /> 3. Ah, sorry, I am a bit new to adversary creation, i thought they mostly had a few skills.<br /> 4. To be fair there is a reason as listed above.<br /> <br /> Honestly I aint even sure if she has a handler or is some sort of independent operator or rogue agent. I should clarify with &quot;Don't plan to move her from Mysterious Ally to Adversary quickly.&quot; you have it a bit backwards, she seems adversarial at first but may become an ally of the band, possibly even a potential romantic interest.<br /> <br /> I apologize tremendously if anything I've said seems rude or dismissive, I promise it was not my intention.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12517-storyteller323","name":"Storyteller323","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-11T18:16:52-07:00","id":1480789,"title":"","content":"Sorry if anything I have said sounded rude, I admit that I am more of the straightforward type so spy stuff is a bit out of my element.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12517-storyteller323","name":"Storyteller323","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}